From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: program the RX DMA burst length and prefetch

The TX side got bgmac's burst and prefetch values in "program the TX DMA
burst length and prefetch"; the RX control word still has none, so the
RX engine runs with 16-byte bursts and no descriptor prefetch.

Program the RX values bgmac uses for the same DMA engine on Northstar
(bgmac_dma_rx_enable(): 128-byte bursts, prefetch 8, threshold 1).
Measured on an EA6900 (BCM4360, 5 GHz VHT80, firmware 784.2) with an
ath11k client, TCP to a wired LAN host: upload 291-324 -> 381-386
Mbit/s, download and 2.4 GHz unchanged, no CCMP replays.

The earlier attempt with these values hit replay drops; that was the
A-MSDU frames that "drop received frames with the A-MSDU bit" now
drops, so the TX patch's "TX only" comment goes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c
@@ -724,8 +724,8 @@
 			 * rates: the FIFO runs dry and the hardware cuts each
 			 * A-MPDU after about 4 frames (BCM4360, 5 GHz VHT80:
 			 * 118 Mbit/s at every width). Use the values bgmac
-			 * programs into the same DMA engine on Northstar. TX only:
-			 * the RX equivalents corrupted received frames.
+			 * programs into the same DMA engine on Northstar; the RX
+			 * side gets them in the RX branch below.
 			 */
 			if (ring->dev->dev->core_rev >= 40)
 				enable |= B43_DMA64_TXMR_2 |
@@ -775,6 +775,16 @@
 			    & B43_DMA64_RXADDREXT_MASK;
 			if (!parity)
 				value |= B43_DMA64_RXPARITYDISABLE;
+			/*
+			 * Out of reset the RX engine also does 16-byte bursts
+			 * without prefetch, which limits what the AC cores can
+			 * receive (BCM4360, 5 GHz VHT80: about 300 Mbit/s up).
+			 * Use bgmac's RX values: 128-byte bursts, prefetch 8,
+			 * threshold 1.
+			 */
+			if (ring->dev->dev->core_rev >= 40)
+				value |= B43_DMA64_RXBURST_128 |
+					 B43_DMA64_RXPREFETCH_8;
 			if (ring->dev->dma.index_is_addr) {
 				value |= b43_dma_read(ring, B43_DMA64_RXCTL) &
 					 B43_DMA64_RXCTL_KEEP;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.h
@@ -124,6 +124,8 @@
 #define		B43_DMA64_RXADDREXT_MASK		0x00030000
 #define		B43_DMA64_RXADDREXT_SHIFT		16
 #define		B43_DMA64_RXCTL_KEEP		0x03FC0000	/* Burst, prefetch */
+#define		B43_DMA64_RXBURST_128			0x000C0000	/* 128-byte bursts */
+#define		B43_DMA64_RXPREFETCH_8			0x00400000	/* Prefetch 8 descriptors */
 #define B43_DMA64_RXINDEX				0x24
 #define B43_DMA64_RXRINGLO				0x28
 #define B43_DMA64_RXRINGHI				0x2C
